hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1574","Ismail bin Bishr bin Mansour Al-Sulami and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, they said: Abd al-A’la told us, Muhammad said: Ubaid told us By God, Ismail said: On the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set out to reconcile Bani Amr bin Awf, and the time for prayer came, so the muezzin came to Abu Bakr, so he ordered him to go ahead of the people and lead them in prayer, so the Messenger of May God bless him and grant him peace. He broke through the rows until he stood in the front row.” Then he mentioned the hadith in its length. This is the wording mentioned in the hadith of Ismail."
